sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as "Operator / Schedule"
    participant Tool as "Inventory Tool (CLI or Lambda)"
    participant Org as "AWS Organization accounts"
    participant AWS as "AWS service APIs"
    participant Config as "AWS Config (optional)"
    participant Health as "AWS Health"
    participant EOL as "EndOfLife.date"
    participant Report as "CSV report + summary"

    User->>Tool: start scan (accounts, regions)

    Tool->>Org: assume read-only role, iterate accounts
    Note over Tool,Org: one account at a time, failures isolated

    loop each account and region
        Tool->>AWS: discover resources and versions (read-only)
        AWS-->>Tool: resources (Lambda, RDS, EKS, MSK, ...)
        opt centralized source available
            Tool->>Config: query inventory (reconcile, not wired)
            Config-->>Tool: resources with provenance
        end
    end

    Note over Tool: normalize into one record model (no invented versions)

    opt lifecycle evaluation (not wired yet)
        Tool->>Health: check AWS-announced end-of-support
        Health-->>Tool: authoritative lifecycle evidence
        Tool->>EOL: look up product/version end-of-life
        EOL-->>Tool: community lifecycle dates
        Note over Tool: precedence Health then EndOfLife, no match means UNKNOWN
    end

    Tool->>Report: write CSV + per-account status
    Report-->>User: inventory.csv + execution summary
